nodecode-artifacts is a rewrite of dmmeteo's dmmeteo/hermes-artifacts:

  https://github.com/dmmeteo/hermes-artifacts
  commit 57b61fca2872d15060d8a9b30b9e51242e9cb357

  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 dmmeteo (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the six agent tools (artifact_publish, artifact_list,
artifact_get, artifact_download, artifact_share, artifact_revoke_share)
against the same /internal/v1 machine API of a self-hosted artifact service,
with the same rules -- publish is private and makes no link, a guest link is
created only when asked, its URL is shown once, links expire and are revoked
by share id, a publish takes a path or inline text and a kind from its
extension, and a download writes the original bytes in one atomic replace.
The original's prose skill is (help :artifacts) here, one line of which
rides every request, and its Hermes profile name became the section's
source_profile label.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes dashboard tab (a React panel and a
FastAPI adapter under the dashboard host) has no counterpart in a Nodecode
cell, so the library's private address is reported as the service's own
/artifacts/<slug> path instead of a dashboard path; Hermes's own read and
write policy hooks are replaced by the section the operator sets; and the
service itself -- a separate application in the same repository -- is not
bundled, as the original did not bundle it either.
